\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Refinement of sites, labels and spin fields}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Let the coarse site group be #{\Lambda=\prod_j\mathbb Z/N_j\mathbb Z} and the fine group #{\Lambda'=\prod_j\mathbb Z/(kN_j)\mathbb Z}, with #{N_j,k} positive integers. The \newvocab{site refinement} sends #{x} to #{\iota(x)=kx}. The \newvocab{restriction of a spin field} with common value space #{S\otimes F} is #{(\iota^*\psi')(x)=\psi'(kx)}. For a scalar character the same formula gives character restriction.}

\p{With spacing #{a'=a/k}, the two grids have the same side lengths. A chosen integer representative #{r_j} at coarse period #{N_j} can be carried to the residue of that same integer modulo #{kN_j}. Its physical wave number #{2\pi r_j/(N_j a)} is unchanged. The choice of an integer at a half-period tie belongs to this carrying convention. Use the \vocabk{translation characters}{fdip-0164} on the site group.}
